"""Battery input, fuse, switch and measurement; the VSYS power path; the 3V3_D buck and the 3V3_A
analog LDO.

Power tree (research/next-revision, Power tree):
- Battery (J1, 4S LiPo, 12.0-16.8 V, 17.4 V with HV cells): BAT_P, then the fuse F1 to VBAT.
  VBAT feeds the motor bridges and the fan driver (drivers sheet) and, through D14, VSYS.
- USB (U2 VBUS, +5V, peripherals sheet): through Q8 to VSYS only. There is no 5 V rail: +5V is
  the VBUS input of the power path, the TVS, and two VBUS-sense dividers.
- VSYS = OR(VBAT, VBUS) feeds only the 3V3_D buck IC7 and, through R58, the 3V3_A LDO U8. So the
  ESP32, the MCU (for SWD flashing) and VDDA all run from USB alone, with the bridges off.

Battery input, fuse and switch. J1 takes the pack: + on BAT_P, - on GND_BAT; the connector keys
the polarity (Q6's body diode conducts with the pack reversed; research Power tree, Battery
switch).
F1 (0501012.WR1, Littelfuse 501 series, Revised 12/14/17, 12 A row: fast-acting, 32 VDC,
3.11 mOhm, melting I2t 20.341 A2s at 1 ms; components/littelfuse/05010xx) carries the whole
battery current from BAT_P to VBAT, so a short on the board (a cracked VBAT capacitor, a failed
bridge) opens it instead of heating copper; only J1 and BAT_P's copper to F1 sit ahead of it.
The row is the lowest that keeps every load inside its ratings (boards/main2/test/test_power.zen
battery_fuse): the battery path's 3-4 A rms (research Drivetrain) against 8.2 A continuous at
75 C (80 % of the rating times the re-rating curve's 0.85, the datasheet's example); the summed
peak limits, both bridges at their 2.97 A ITRIP, the fan at its 3.94 A limit (drivers sheet) and
the 3V3 rails, 10.1 A, against 10.2 A (100 % of the rating, held 4 hours minimum, times 0.85), so
even a stall burst that lasted would not open it. On the Average Time Current Curves (digitised
from the datasheet's vector paths) a 10.1 A burst is far from opening it (28 A in 100 s, 24 A at
75 C), and as a repeated pulse it uses (10.1 / 24)^2 = 18 % of the melting I2t at that duration,
within the 22 % that withstands 100,000 pulses (Littelfuse Fuseholder Rerating, Chart II, Pulse
Cycle Withstand Capability). The largest pulse at plug-in or switch-on is under 0.01 A2s (Q6 stays
off at plug-in, below; vbat_bulk.py section 8). Against the 20 A row it clears partial faults
sooner: 40 A in about 0.4 s (20 A row: about 100 s), 50 A in about 0.06 s (about 5 s), 30 A in
about 24 s (the 20 A row does not open below 40 A in 100 s). The 10 A row (6.8 A continuous at
75 C) carries the rms budget too, but not the summed peak limits at 75 C (8.5 A). Every row
interrupts 150 A at 32 VDC (note 1: at the rated voltage, time constant < 0.5 ms) and has the same
1206 body; 16 mV and 66 mW at 4 A at most (the 49.27 mV drop at 12 A taken as a resistance). A
1206 part (0.835 mm high) because F1 sits under the chassis's 1.5 mm tail_right zone
(spec/main2.toml).
The pack's short circuit stays inside those 150 A. Cells in series all carry the one current, so
a 4S pack shorts at VCELL / RCELL whatever its cell count: the 4.35 V of a full HV cell over its
ohmic resistance. The lowest published for cells of the pack's class is 52.8 mOhm (a 1S 180 mAh
cell; small 1S cells of 100-220 mAh measure 52.8-131 mOhm on an AC meter, Takeyuta Lab,
neophile.hatenablog.com/entry/2023/08/19/143147), which gives 82 A before the leads, J1 (10 mOhm
per contact, JST PA catalogue) and F1 add their own. 150 A would need cells below 29 mOhm, the
class of 300 mAh and larger high-rate packs, outside the board's 4S <= 180 mAh pack (research
Power tree, Battery input).
J1 is a JST PA header: 3 A AC/DC with AWG #22, contact resistance 10 mOhm max, -25 to +85 C
including the temperature rise from the current (JST PA catalogue, epa0125). The battery path
carries about 2.6 A mean and at most 3 A rms over a fast run (the firmware's limit, research
Drivetrain) with 5-6 A peaks under 1 s, so its rms stays inside the rating with AWG #22 pack
leads.
A reversed pack (against the key) forward-biases D15 from GND_BAT into VBAT, a short through F1,
which opens; until then the board sees only the difference between D15's drop and Q6's
body-diode drop. D15 need not survive it (IFSM 60 A for 8.3 ms, SMAJ series p1).
Q6 (HSBB3072, 30 V N-MOSFET) is a low-side switch from GND_BAT to GND; SW4 drives its gate from
VBAT through R43 100 kOhm with R41 100 kOhm to GND_BAT, so VGS settles at VBAT / 2 = 6.0-8.7 V
(RDS(on) 3.8 mOhm max at 4.5 V, HSBB3072 p2), inside +-20 V; VDS 30 V is 1.72x the 17.4 V pack.
Its gate network keeps it off when the pack is plugged in and slews it when SW4 turns it on:
- Plug-in: the pack's edge lands on Q6's drain (the board's GND, held to VBAT by the bulk) and
  reaches the gate through the gate-drain capacitance, C114 1 nF C0G plus Q6's own Crss (10.7 nC
  from 0 to 24.2 V, Fig. 7); C58 100 nF from gate to source holds it: at most 0.40 V at the
  24.2 V clamp, below VGS(th) min 1.0 V (p2), and below the 0.75 V it falls to at 85 C (Fig. 5) for
  the 17.4 V pack (test_power.zen plug_in_keeps_q6_off). Q6 stays off, the board sees no edge
  (VBAT slews 0.002 V/us at most), and the pack charges only Q6's output capacitance, which
  rings Q6's VDS to at most 23.9 V, under D15's clamp and the 30 V rating. With C58 alone from
  gate to drain, as on the main board, the edge turned Q6 on at 3.3-3.6 V and VBAT slewed at
  1.3-2.0 V/us at 89-135 A, above the STSPIN958's 0.5 V/us dVS/dt absolute maximum (DS14341
  Table 1).
- SW4 on: the gate charges through R43 || R41 (50 kOhm) to the plateau, and VBAT starts rising
  1.7 ms after SW4 closes; then C114 + Crss set the slew, IG / CGD <= 17.4 V / (100 kOhm x
  1.23 nF) = 0.14 V/us, under the 0.5 V/us (test_power.zen battery_switch_slew). Simulated, VBAT
  rises 10-90 % in 0.40 ms at 0.042 V/us with a 5.8 A load, with 51 W peak and 21 mJ in Q6,
  inside its SOA (Fig. 8: about 130 W for 1 ms at TC 25 C).
- SW4 off: the gate falls through R41 to the plateau, and VBAT starts falling 12.9 ms after SW4
  opens, then falls in 2.1 ms under a 5.8 A load at 0.008 V/us: no inductive kick. (Simulated with
  Q6's model fitted to its typical curves, vbat_bulk.py Q6_MODEL: Miller plateau 2.8 V at 20 A.)
A 2.2 uF gate-source capacitor with C58 left from gate to drain also keeps Q6 off, but delays
switch-on by 36 ms and switch-off by 270 ms (vbat_bulk.py section 8).
SW4 is the SK-12D29-G060 (G-Switch drawing SK-12D29-GXXX): DC 24 V 1.0 A, 1.38x the 17.4 V
pack; it carries only the gate drive (VBAT / 200 kOhm = 87 uA). Its body is the main board's
MK-12D18 size (8.6 x 3.6 x 3.6 mm) with a 6.0 mm black lever over the rear notch's edge; three
pins at 2.0 mm pitch and two frame legs (components/g-switch/SK-12D29-G060).
TVS, D15 (SMAJ18A, Littelfuse SMAJ series p2: VR 18 V, VBR 20.0-22.1 V at 1 mA, VC 29.2 V at
13.7 A, 400 W 10/1000 us), behind F1: cathode on VBAT, anode on GND_BAT, so a TVS that fails
short (its failure mode when over-stressed, p1) opens F1. VR is above the 17.4 V
pack (IR 1 uA max). With the pack pulled while the bridges brake, the motors push up to 3.8 W into
VBAT (research Power tree, VBAT overvoltage), which the VBAT ceramics alone hold below the
DRV8874's 40 V for only about 12 ms. D15 takes that current from VBAT and returns it to GND through
Q6, in both of Q6's states: with SW4 on, through its channel (VGS = VBAT / 2);
with SW4 off, through its body diode, whose forward direction is GND_BAT to GND (VSD 1.2 V max at
1 A, HSBB3072 p2). VBAT then sits at VBR plus D15's slope, plus the body-diode drop with SW4 off:
21.2-22.4 V with SW4 on and 21.9-23.1 V off for 0.15-2 A of braking current (simulated at a
21 V knee; up to 1.1 V more at the 22.1 V VBR maximum): 24.2 V at most, below every rating on
VBAT, VSYS and LDO_IN (the 50 V MLCCs, Q6's and Q8's 30 V, the 32 V fuse and the 40 V parts;
test_power.zen abs_max_under_clamp). It also clamps Q6's VDS and a bench-supply hot plug (24.2 V unclamped, 23.5 V
clamped from 17.4 V on 1 m leads). Research calculations/power_tree/vbat_bulk.py.
SW4's ON position is the lever at the B end (pin 3, x = +2 mm on the footprint). The slider
carries the moving contact under the lever, so the lever's end of the travel joins the common to
the outer pin on that end, and the drawing agrees: its end view draws the lever at one end of its
2 mm travel, offset 1.0 mm towards one outer pin, and its SCHEMATIC, drawn in the same
orientation, joins the common to that same-side terminal with the solid (closed) line and to the
other with the dashed (open) one (SK-12D29-GXXX; the C&K SK series schematic likewise pairs
position 1 with pins 1-2 and position 2 with pins 2-3). A reversed reading would only swap the
silkscreen's ON and OFF: the circuit works in either case and the board shows at once whether
it is on.


Battery measurement: R44 10 kOhm / R45 2 kOhm from VBAT into Battery_Voltage (PC5, ADC12_INP8,
DS13311 Table 8; a slow channel, Table 85 notes 4-5) with C59 100 nF: 17.4 V x 2 / 12 = 2.90 V at
the HV pack's top, below VDDA (the main board's 27 kOhm gives 3.70 V, above it); Thevenin
1.67 kOhm with 100 nF (0.17 ms) holds the pin for the ADC sample and takes the 100 kHz ripple
(265 mV pp on VBAT) down to 0.4 mV pp at the pin. The firmware divides by 12 / 2 = 6.0
(boards/main2/firmware_changes.toml). The divider draws 1.45 mA from the pack with SW4 on (none
with SW4 off: Q6 opens its return); R44 dissipates 21 mW at 17.4 V and 41 mW at the 24.2 V clamp,
inside the 0402's 62.5 mW. It is this low to hold VBAT down on USB alone: with the pack absent or
switched off, nothing else ties VBAT to GND, and D14's reverse leakage from VSYS (140 uA at 85 C,
below) plus Q6's (pack fitted, SW4 off: 1 uA at 25 C and 5 uA at 55 C max, HSBB3072 p2, 25 uA at
85 C at that rate) lifts it to I x 11.9 kOhm (R44 + R45 with R56 + R57) = 2.0 V, so Q8's gate
stays 2.5 V below a 4.4 V VBUS (test_power.zen usb_only_vbat_float). With 100 kOhm / 20 kOhm the
same leakage would lift VBAT towards VSYS above about 50-60 C and turn Q8 off, leaving USB to
feed VSYS through its body diode, 0.7 V lower.

Power path (research A.4; power-tree study section 8):
- VBAT -> VSYS: D14, B5819W 40 V 1 A Schottky (JCET B5817W-B5819W p1: VRRM 40 V, VF 0.6 V max at
  1 A). The 17.4 V pack is 44 % of VRRM. Forward (p2 Forward Characteristics, typical): about
  0.32 V at 25 C and 0.23 V at 100 C at the 0.13 A it carries at 14.8 V (40 mW), 0.48 / 0.43 V at
  1 A. Reverse (p2 Reverse Characteristics, typical, read at 1-5 V): 5-6 uA at 25 C, 55-64 uA at
  75 C, 0.42-0.59 mA at 100 C, so about 140 uA at 85 C between those curves; 12 uA / 0.11 mA /
  0.92 mA at 17 V. It blocks VSYS -> VBAT; its leakage then feeds VBAT (battery measurement above).
- VBUS -> VSYS: Q8, AO3401A P-MOSFET (Rev 3.1 p1: -30 V VDS, +-12 V VGS absolute maximum), drain
  on +5V, source on VSYS, so its body diode conducts VBUS -> VSYS and blocks VSYS -> VBUS. The
  gate follows VBAT through R56 10 kOhm with R57 1 MOhm to GND: with the pack on, the gate sits at
  0.99 VBAT and VSYS one Schottky drop below VBAT, so VGS = VF - 0.01 VBAT, -0.17 to +0.48 V over
  any VF from 0 to D14's 0.6 V maximum: off (VGS(th) -0.5 to -1.3 V, p2), whatever D14's forward
  drop does with temperature; with the pack off or absent, the gate falls towards GND (2.0 V at
  most, battery measurement above) and VGS is -2.4 to -5.5 V, on. A 4S pack
  (>= 12 V) is always above VBUS (<= 5.5 V), so the battery always wins and USB never back-feeds
  VBAT; with the battery on, VSYS never reaches VBUS.
- D16 (BZT52C10S, 10 V zener, Diodes DS30093: VZ 9.4-10.6 V at 5 mA, IR 0.1 uA at 7 V) from Q8's
  gate (anode) to VSYS (cathode) clamps VGS. When VBAT falls faster than VSYS (a VBAT short, the
  pack pulled or SW4 opened under load), the gate follows VBAT down while C52/C53/C80 hold VSYS
  up: without D16 VGS reaches -15 to -16 V (-11 to -13 V with a 10 uF C63), past the 12 V, until
  Q8 has dumped VSYS into +5V. With D16 it stays within -10.6 V, at 0.7 mA through R56
  (vbat_bulk.py section 9). Its 9.4 V minimum is above the -5.5 V of USB-only operation, where it
  leaks at most 0.1 uA; with the pack on it sits forward-biased by at most 0.48 V, below its
  forward knee, and draws next to nothing. It thus also bounds VGS at about +0.7 V on the
  positive side.
- C63 1 uF on +5V. USB 2.0 (section 7.2.4.1) allows a device 10 uF at attach; VSYS's C52 10 uF
  and C53 1 uF, and C80 10 uF behind R58, also charge through Q8's body diode: 22 uF nominal in
  all, an accepted excess (Q8's body diode leaves no inrush limit possible; most hosts tolerate
  it), bounded by test_power.zen usb_attach_capacitance.
- VSYS: 4.3-17.4 V (USB-only at 4.4 V minus the FET; the pack minus D14).
- USB budget: the board reads no Type-C current advertisement (its CC pins carry only the Rd
  pull-downs), so it takes what a Default-advertising USB 2.0 port gives a configured device,
  500 mA (Type-C R2.5 sections 2.3.4 and 4.6.2.1; USB 2.0 Table 7-7). USB alone is for flashing,
  debug and telemetry (222-441 mA, research Power tree); the firmware keeps the emitters, LEDs and
  motors off or dim there (firmware_changes.toml esp, usb_only). Reading Rp for 1.5 / 3 A would buy
  only the emitters and LEDs on USB, which a robot on the bench does not need, at the cost of
  sensing both CC lines (Table 4-36's vRd levels) on two more ADC inputs.

3V3_D buck, IC7 (L6981C33DR, fixed 3.3 V, low-consumption mode, DS13554), as on the main board:
VIN and EN on VSYS. Integrator parts per DS13554 Table 1 p3 and Table 2 p4: C55 100 nF BOOT to
SW; C54 1 uF on VCC; L3 22 uH (YSPIA0645-220M, 4.5 A Isat); C52 10 uF 50 V X7R 1210 + C53 1 uF
50 V X7R 0805 on VSYS at IC7 (CIN 10 uF typ). Eq. 35, CIN,min = IOUT / (4 x VPP x fSW) with VPP
5 % of VIN,max (section 8.4.1): 1.5 A / (4 x 0.87 V x 360 kHz) = 1.2 uF; C52 keeps 5.9 uF at
17.4 V (Samsung DC-bias curve, passives.zen DC_BIAS), 5.3 uF less its tolerance. Both are 50 V
parts: at most 35 % of the rating at 17.4 V and 48 % at the 24.2 V clamp (the 60 % derating of
NASA PD-ED-1201; test_power.zen capacitor_voltage_derating); C56/C57 22 uF on 3V3_D. Ripple by Eq. 36 at fSW 400 kHz typ (Table 6):
(17.4 - 3.3) x 3.3 / (17.4 x 22 uH x 400 kHz) = 0.30 A at the top of the HV pack, 20 % of the
1.5 A rating (the section 8.4.2 target is 20-40 %). Slope compensation: 22 uH is ST's own
inductor for VOUT 3.3 V (section 10, Fig. 40-45 at VIN 12 and 24 V, 400 kHz: MSS1038T-223ML with
22 uF + 10 uF). Eq. 38's 0.4 <= QP <= 1.33 with ISLOPE = 1 A (Eq. 11, 13) is not met as written by
any configuration ST publishes (QP 0.33 at 12 V for that 3.3 V design, 0.27-0.38 for the 5 V
33 uH one), and the "full slope contribution" current limit (1.55 A against 2.0 A, Table 6)
implies a ramp of about 0.45 A. Either way L3 cannot oscillate sub-harmonically: the current
loop's perturbation factor (Se - Sf) / (Sn + Se) stays below 1 in magnitude for any ISLOPE above
0.12 A at the worst point (4.3 V, 440 kHz), and is at most 0.6 at 0.45 A or 1 A; below 12 V the
duty is under 0.5 and needs no ramp at all. A QP below 0.4 only damps the loop more (27-33 deg of
sampling lag at 40 kHz on the pack with ISLOPE = 1 A, 20 deg at 0.45 A, 49 deg at 4.3 V, USB
only). 33 uH is lower in QP everywhere, and about 10 uH would meet Eq. 38 literally at 40-50 %
ripple, above the 20-40 % target (research calculations/power_tree/l6981_slope.py).
test_power.zen buck_slope_compensation checks the upper bound and L3 <= 33 uH. Every capacitor on 3V3_D must stay inside the
30.5-145 uF window of Eq. 42/43 (boards/main2/test/test_power.zen). In LCM the buck skips pulses
at light load (section 6.4.1, +1.8 %); the analog loads are on 3V3_A, so that step no longer
reaches the ADC.

3V3_A analog LDO, U8 (ADP7142ACPZN3.3-R7, fixed 3.3 V, 2.7-40 V input, ADP7142 Rev K), chosen over the TPS7A4901 (fixed output with no feedback
divider, lower noise, specified EN thresholds; research Open decisions):
- Input RC: R58 22 Ohm from VSYS to LDO_IN with C80 10 uF 50 V X7R 1210 (research A.4). It keeps the 100 kHz
  motor ripple out of the LDO (68 dB PSRR at 100 kHz, 50 dB at 1 MHz, Table 1) and leaves
  headroom on USB alone: 4.3 V - 22 Ohm x 23 mA = 3.8 V, above 3.3 V + 40 mV dropout at 25 mA
  (Figure 22).
- C81 10 uF on 3V3_A (Table 2: effective >= 1.5 uF over the operating conditions; with more than
  2.2 uF on the output, the input capacitor matches it: 10 uF each). Eq. 4 (CEFF = CBIAS x
  (1 - TEMPCO) x (1 - TOL), TEMPCO 15 %) with the Samsung DC-bias curves (passives.zen DC_BIAS):
  C81 keeps 6.5 uF at 3.36 V, x 0.85 x 0.8 (its 20 %) = 4.4 uF; C80 keeps 5.9 uF at 17.4 V (7.4 uF
  at 12 V), x 0.85 x 0.9 = 4.5 uF; both above 1.5 uF, and the input's effective capacitance
  matches the output's within 10 % at the HV pack's top. The Samsung TCC curves of both parts stay
  within -12 % over -40 to 85 C, inside the 15 %.
- EN on 3V3_D: 3V3_A starts after VDD (EN on threshold 1.30 V max, off 1.06 V min, Table 1), so
  VDDA never leads VDD at power-up (DS13311 section 3.7.1, Figure 2). SS open: the internal
  380 us start-up (pin table; never ground SS).
- Loads (research, Power tree): VDDA through R67, U10/U11 INA241A2 VS and REF1, the four
  phototransistor collectors, the emitter-sink op-amp U12 and its 200 kOhm bias: 9.7 mA typical,
  22.5 mA worst case (research calculations/power_tree/calc_power_tree.py section 1: both ADCs
  at DS13311 Table 84's per-ADC maximum, the DAC's 20 + 160 uA from VDDA and VREF+, Table 90).
- Heat: worst case (Eq. 10) 14.1 V x 22.5 mA + 17.4 V x 190 uA = 0.32 W, at the HV pack's top
  with every receiver saturated; 0.11 W typical (9.7 mA from 14.8 V). The exposed pad sits on the
  F.Cu GND pour with two GND vias within 1.6 mm to the In1/In2 GND planes (3500-3700 mm2 each),
  more copper than Table 6's 500 mm2 row (83.9 C/W; 71.7 C/W at 1000 mm2, 182.8 C/W on minimum
  traces) and close to Table 4's JEDEC 4-layer 72.1 C/W: at 83.9 C/W the junction sits at
  85 + 27 = 112 C at an 85 C ambient, inside the 125 C limit (p17), and 15 K above the board
  under it (PsiJB 47.1 C/W, Table 4). Figures 53-54 draw the 500 mm2 line at about
  143 C/W, which would give 131 C at an 85 C ambient, still 19 K below the 150 C thermal shutdown
  and inside 125 C up to a 79 C ambient. Keep the LDO away from the IMU.
- Output: 3.24-3.36 V over load, line and -40 to 125 C (Table 1, +-1.8 %); -1.2 / +1.5 % to
  85 C. Its drift is a typical curve only: Figure 16 (VOUT = 3.3 V) moves about -0.1 % from 25 to
  65 C and -0.12 % to 85 C, so a per-board calibration at room temperature leaves about 0.1 % over
  a 40 K swing; the datasheet guarantees no tempco. The firmware can bound it by reading VREFINT
  (DS13311 Table 21: 70 ppm/C max, 0.28 % over 40 K).
"""

load(
    "./passives.zen",
    "C_100N_0402",
    "C_10U_0603",
    "C_10U_1210_50V",
    "C_1N_0402_C0G",
    "C_1U_0402",
    "C_1U_0805_50V",
    "C_22U_0805_25V",
    "R_100K_0402",
    "R_10K_0402",
    "R_1M_0402",
    "R_22_0402",
    "R_2K_0402",
)

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")
Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")
ADP7142 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/adi/ADP7142/ADP7142.zen")
AO3401A = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/aos/AO3401A/AO3401A.zen")
B02B_PASK = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/jst/B02B-PASK/B02B-PASK.zen")
BZT52C10S = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/diodes/BZT52C10S/BZT52C10S.zen")
FUSE_501 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/littelfuse/05010xx/05010xx.zen")
B5819W = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/cj/B5819W/B5819W.zen")
HSBB3072 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/huashuo/HSBB3072/HSBB3072.zen")
L6981 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/st/L6981/L6981.zen")
SK_12D29_G060 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/g-switch/SK-12D29-G060/SK-12D29-G060.zen")
SMAJ18A = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/littelfuse/SMAJ18A/SMAJ18A.zen")
YSPIA0645_220M = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/yjycoin/YSPIA0645-220M/YSPIA0645-220M.zen")

# Its own sheet in the board schematic (layout/main2.kicad_sch).
Project(name="Regulators", path="layout", layout=False)

# A signal port takes the name of the board net it carries (the firmware's pin label) wherever
# that name is an identifier, so its sheet pin and hierarchical label match the root's label:
# KiCad's ERC flags labels whose names differ only in case (similar_labels).
BAT_P = io(Power)
VBAT = io(Power)
VSYS = io(Power)
V3V3_D = io(Power)
V3V3_A = io(Power)
V5V = io(Power)
GND = io(Ground)
GND_BAT = io(Ground)
Battery_Voltage = io(Net)

BAT_SW_DRIVE = Net("BAT_SW_DRIVE")
BAT_SW_GATE = Net("BAT_SW_GATE")
PATH_GATE = Net("PATH_GATE")
BUCK_SW = Net("BUCK_SW")
BUCK_BOOT = Net("BUCK_BOOT")
# The L6981 VCC LDO output, 3.3 V typ (DS13554 Table 6 p7).
BUCK_VCC = Power("BUCK_VCC", voltage="3.0V to 3.6V")
# The LDO input after R58: VSYS less 22 Ohm x 23 mA at most.
LDO_IN = Power("LDO_IN", voltage="3.8V to 17.4V")

# Battery input, fuse and switch.
B02B_PASK(name="J1", prefix="J", P1=BAT_P, P2=GND_BAT)
FUSE_501(name="F1", rating="12A", P1=BAT_P, P2=VBAT)
SMAJ18A(name="D15", K=VBAT, A=GND_BAT)
SK_12D29_G060(name="SW4", A=NotConnected(), COM=VBAT, B=BAT_SW_DRIVE)
Resistor(name="R43", P1=BAT_SW_DRIVE, P2=BAT_SW_GATE, **R_100K_0402)
HSBB3072(
    name="Q6",
    paste="split",  # open thermal vias in the drain pad: its paste in windows round them
    G=BAT_SW_GATE,
    S=GND_BAT,
    D=GND,
)
